      "claim": "AZD0837, a proline-amide peptidomimetic, has absolute oral bioavailability 22–55% in humans, directly above the 20% threshold; L2 confirms the same range.",
      "card_ids": ["C01", "C04", "C30", "C47"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Acalabrutinib, sharing proline-amide-to-heteroaromatic connectivity, has absolute F ~25% in humans; L2 dog and formulation data are consistent with F ≥ 20%.",
      "card_ids": ["C02", "C12", "C21", "C22", "C29", "C32", "C33", "C40", "C44", "C53", "C58", "C67"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "Compound 5 and MMV367, other proline/azetidine amide compounds, report F 41% and 90%; L2 confirms MMV367 oral bioavailability in preclinical models.",
      "card_ids": ["C07", "C23", "C26", "C60", "C61"]
    },
    {
      "claim": "No transferable direct outcome supports F < 20% for the query; the only low absolute F in L2 is maraviroc in rat (6%), which is species-specific and not structurally relevant.",
      "card_ids": ["C43"]
    }
  ],
  "new_evidence_assessment": [
    {
