        "C47", "C32", "C33", "C39", "C40", "C44", "C48", "C51", "C53", "C58", "C67", "C60", "C61"
      ]
    }
  ],
  "evidence_gaps": [
    "No direct oral bioavailability measurement exists for the query molecule.",
    "No context matches the exact dimeric bis-imidazole/bis-carbamate scaffold; query MW 738.9, TPSA 174.6, and logP 6.22 are substantially larger/more polar than the high-F context molecules.",
    "No query-specific measured solubility, permeability, first-pass, or efflux data are available; the low physicochemical prior is predicted, not measured.",
    "L2 shows species/formulation dependence in some contexts (e.g., maraviroc rat F = 6%; asciminib high-fat food effect; delavirdine dog milled-quality), but these are not query-specific and do not provide affirmative low evidence for the query.",
    "Transferability of the high-F contexts is uncertain because of size and polarity differences."
  ],
  "decision_summary": "L2 adds further high-F records for the most structurally relevant proline-amide/heteroaromatic contexts (AZD0837, acalabrutinib, MMV367) and no affirmative threshold-relevant low evidence for the query; the unfavorable physicochemical prior is a predicted liability, not an endpoint measurement, so F ≥ 20% remains better supported."
}

